Kind: ablation
Issue: #598
Takes out: the claim's range check -- the pin count again, which says nothing about a GSI below the controller's first pin, so ISA 4 is routed into redir_reg()'s panic
Run: --entry 0 600 -smp 1
Expect: ioapic: asked about a pin this controller does not own

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/cpu/device_machdep.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/cpu/device_machdep.c
--- a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/cpu/device_machdep.c
+++ b/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/cpu/device_machdep.c
@@ -497,7 +497,7 @@
 	 * say that ISA 0 arrives on GSI 2, and on a PC it does.
 	 */
 	gsi = acpi_irq_to_gsi((uint8_t)irq);
-	if (!ioapic_owns(gsi))		/* the range, not the count: #598's C12 */
+	if (gsi >= ioapic_pin_count())
 		return 0;
 	if (!irq_target(&target))	/* C16, #659 */
 		return 0;
